ut wait, maybe there\'s more to it. Could the context change the result? For example, in different number systems or under certain conditions like modular arithmetic? Hmm, let\'s explore that a bit.\n\nFirst off, in standard base 10 mathematics, which is what we usually use daily, 1 plus 1 definitely equals 2. There\'s no ambiguity there. It\'s one of the foundational truths of math.\n\nBut if I think about different numeral systems, like binary or hexadecimal, things might look different. In binary, for instance, adding 1 and 1 gives a carry-over. Let me check that: in binary, 1 plus 1 equals 10. So, in base 2, the sum is represented as \'10\', which translates back to our decimal system as 2. So essentially, it\'s still the same value.\n\nIn hexadecimal, adding 1 and 1 would also give 2 because hexadecimal uses digits up to 15 before rolling over, but since we\'re only adding single units here, there\'s no rollover needed either. So again, 1 plus 1 equals 2 in hexadecimal.\n\nWhat about other contexts? Like when dealing with sets or','',_binary '','',NULL,NULL,'1','2025-11-19 11:53:44','1','2025-11-19 11:53:54',_binary '\0',1),(3303,1781604279872581828,NULL,1,NULL,'user','deepseek-r1',26,'1+1=？',NULL,_binary '','',NULL,NULL,'1','2025-11-19 11:53:46','1','2025-11-19 16:47:09',_binary '',1),(3304,1781604279872581828,3303,1,NULL,'assistant','deepseek-r1',26,'<think>','',_binary '','',NULL,NULL,'1','2025-11-19 11:53:46','1','2025-11-19 16:46:58',_binary '',1),(3305,1781604279872581811,NULL,1,19,'user','deepseek-reasoner',18,'搜下百度',NULL,_binary '','',NULL,'','1','2025-11-19 19:05:06','1','2025-11-19 19:05:06',_binary '\0',1),(3306,1781604279872581811,3305,1,19,'assistant','deepseek-reasoner',18,'您可以通过以下方式使用百度搜索：\n\n1. **访问官网**：在浏览器地址栏输入 www.baidu.com 进入百度首页\n\n2. **进行搜索**：\n   - 在搜索框中输入您想查找的关键词\n   - 点击\"百度一下\"按钮或按回车键\n   - 系统会显示相关的搜索结果\n\n3. **搜索技巧**：\n   - 使用更具体的关键词可以获得更精确的结果\n   - 如果找不到想要的内容，可以尝试更换相似的关键词\n   - 使用引号\"\"可以搜索完整短语\n   - 使用减号-可以排除某些词语\n\n百度提供网页、图片、